      "problem": "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(A).$",
      "worked_solution": "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(8-(-3))\\cdot (-5-1) \\\\  & =11\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =-66.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
